{
  "note": "The shared truth for every cerno SDK. `requests` pin the JSON a client must produce from a given builder call; `responses` pin the values a client must read back out; `errors` pin the failure mapping; `unknown_codes` are errors in cerno's shape with a code newer than the client, which must keep that code; `unexpected` are bodies that are not cerno's at all, sent verbatim as `body_text`, which every client reports as an unexpected response rather than guessing at them. The third response case is an answer read off letters the model was not going to write: its `label_mass` is what gives that away. Each SDK runs all of them against a mock server. The Rust test suite additionally checks every body here against the server's own types, so a case can never describe something the service would reject.",
